// PROPOSED, UNIMPLEMENTED AND UNTESTED. Not applied to the original report and never run or compiled.
// Written as suggested corrections; validate in Power BI Desktop on a copy before any use.
// This file is a catalog of individual Desktop measure definitions, not one
// executable DAX query. Paste one Name = Expression block per measure.
// No model evaluation or Desktop compilation has been performed here.

// ============================================================================
// A. READY-TO-APPLY RENAMES: unchanged business arithmetic and filter behavior.
// Rename existing objects in Desktop to preserve their identities/bindings.
// These blocks show the final expressions AFTER the listed dependency renames.
// Rename the row-count/store-count helpers first, then their dependents.
// Keep Total Sales, Online Sales and Total Online Customers unchanged.
// BLANK handling is intentionally unchanged. DISTINCTCOUNT includes BLANK;
// purchasing-customer/store descriptions do not establish key completeness.
// ============================================================================

// Home table: FactSales. Rename existing [Total Transactions]. Format: 0.
FactSales Row Count =
COUNTROWS(FactSales)

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Rename existing [Online Transactions]. Format: 0.
Online Fact Row Count =
COUNTROWS(FactOnlineSales)

// Home table: FactSales. Rename existing [Avg Order Value].
// Revenue per stored FactSales row; no claim of order or transaction grain.
Sales per FactSales Row =
DIVIDE([Total Sales], [FactSales Row Count])

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Rename existing [Avg Order Online Value].
Online Sales per Fact Row =
DIVIDE([Online Sales], COUNTROWS(FactOnlineSales))

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Rename existing [Avg Customer LTV].
// Revenue per distinct CustomerKey represented in the filtered online facts.
// Retains date/product/store/age filters; neither lifetime nor predicted value.
Online Sales per Purchasing Customer =
DIVIDE([Online Sales], [Total Online Customers])

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Rename existing [Avg Orders per Customer].
Online Fact Rows per Purchasing Customer =
DIVIDE(COUNTROWS(FactOnlineSales), [Total Online Customers])

// Home table: FactSales. Rename existing [Online %].
// A ratio of two fact-table revenue measures, NOT a combined-sales share.
// Values can exceed 1. Do not label FactSales as exclusively in-store/offline:
// channelKey remains present and fact overlap has not been established.
Online Sales to FactSales Sales Ratio =
DIVIDE(FactOnlineSales[Online Sales], [Total Sales])

// Home table: FactSales. Rename existing [Store Count]. Format: 0.
// Distinct StoreKey values represented in the current FactSales filter context.
// Not the full DimStore roster, open-store count, or count of positive-sales stores.
Store Keys Represented in FactSales =
DISTINCTCOUNT(FactSales[StoreKey])

// Home table: FactSales. Rename existing [Avg Sales per Store].
Sales per Represented Store Key =
DIVIDE([Total Sales], [Store Keys Represented in FactSales])

// Home table: FactSales. Rename existing [Sales per Transaction].
// This duplicates Sales per FactSales Row arithmetically. Retain the object until
// all usages are checked; this package does not delete or consolidate measures.
FactSales Revenue per Row =
DIVIDE([Total Sales], [FactSales Row Count])

// ============================================================================
// B. OPTIONAL SCALE STANDARDIZATION: use only after inspecting visual overrides.
// No observed formatting bug is asserted. Current Customer % and Sales % return
// fractions; Total Sales % and Store % return the equivalent fractions * 100.
// Their recovered model FormatString is null; visual formatting remains unknown.
// Either keep legacy 0..100-style values with an ordinary numeric format and
// clearly labeled percentage units, OR adopt these fraction measures with 0.0%.
// Do not apply an automatic percent multiplier to the legacy *100 values.
// Do not overwrite legacy measures until thresholds, tooltips, axes, exports,
// conditional formatting, and all consumers have been reconciled.
// Negative/offsetting sales can produce ratios outside the usual 0..1 range.
// ============================================================================

// Home table: FactSales. New optional measure. Format: 0.0%.
// Equals original [Total Sales %] / 100 wherever the denominator is defined.
FactSales Sales Share by State =
DIVIDE(
    SUM(FactSales[SalesAmount]),
    CALCULATE(SUM(FactSales[SalesAmount]), ALL(DimGeography[StateProvinceName]))
)

// Home table: FactSales. New optional measure. Format: 0.0%.
// Equals original [Store %] / 100. Retains all other geography/date filters.
Represented Store Key Share by State =
DIVIDE(
    DISTINCTCOUNT(FactSales[StoreKey]),
    CALCULATE(
        DISTINCTCOUNT(FactSales[StoreKey]),
        ALL(DimGeography[StateProvinceName])
    )
)

// ============================================================================
// C. CONDITIONAL ORDER DEFINITIONS. DO NOT APPLY TO THE CURRENT EXTRACTED MODEL.
// SalesOrderNumber and SalesOrderLineNumber currently do not exist in that model.
// First retain both through the M proposal and refresh only the working copy.
// Gate: establish source order grain; SalesOrderNumber must identify exactly one
// business order across customers/stores/time, with no blank or empty identifiers.
// Repeated order numbers across lines are expected; repeated independent orders
// under one number are not. Validate (order number, line number) grain separately.
// Do not guess a composite order key or count OnlineSalesKey as an order ID.
// Verify SalesAmount is additive at the loaded row grain, not repeated order total.
// If any gate fails, keep Section A names and do not use the following formulas.
// ============================================================================

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Conditional. Format: 0.
Validated Online Order Count =
DISTINCTCOUNT(FactOnlineSales[SalesOrderNumber])

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Conditional on the count above.
// Counts orders with at least one fact row in current context. Product or date
// filters can leave only part of an order's revenue. This is selected-row revenue
// per represented order, not automatically full-basket AOV under all slicers.
Online Sales per Represented Order =
DIVIDE([Online Sales], [Validated Online Order Count])

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Conditional on validated customer/order keys.
Online Orders per Purchasing Customer =
DIVIDE([Validated Online Order Count], [Total Online Customers])

// No FactSales distinct-order measure is supplied: no evidenced order ID exists.

// ============================================================================
// D. CONDITIONAL COMBINED-SALES SHARE. Separate proposal, never a rename of Online %.
// Gate: prove fact revenue populations are disjoint, consistently valued in the
// same currency and time scope, and legitimately additive without double counting.
// Verify filter alignment: shared Date/Product/Store filters reach both facts,
// but DimCustomer filters reach only FactOnlineSales in the recovered model.
// Restrict the visual to comparable shared filters unless a separate population
// design is approved. Do not silently remove or ignore asymmetric filters.
// If FactSales already includes online sales, do not use this denominator.
// ============================================================================

// Home table: FactOnlineSales. Conditional new measure. Format: 0.0%.
Online Share of Validated Combined Sales =
DIVIDE([Online Sales], [Online Sales] + [Total Sales])

// ============================================================================
// E. CONDITIONAL AGE VISUAL MEASURES: choose a policy, not both by default.
// Use only after the corresponding new M columns exist. Remove the old Agegroup
// axis/slicers/filters from these visuals; keep raw age columns out of filter UI.
// Each denominator removes only its chosen age-band filter, retaining other scope.
// Existing Customer % / Sales % remove the OLD DimCustomer[Agegroup] filter and
// must not simply be reused with a different age-band column.
// ============================================================================

// Fixed-date alternative: home FactOnlineSales. Format each as 0.0%.
Online Customer Share by Fixed-Date Age =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Online Customers],
    CALCULATE(
        [Total Online Customers],
        REMOVEFILTERS(DimCustomer[AgeGroupAsOfDate])
    )
)

Online Sales Share by Fixed-Date Age =
DIVIDE(
    [Online Sales],
    CALCULATE([Online Sales], REMOVEFILTERS(DimCustomer[AgeGroupAsOfDate]))
)

// Purchase-age alternative: home FactOnlineSales. Format each as 0.0%.
// A customer can appear in multiple purchase-age bands across a long period.
// Customer reach percentages can total more than 100%; this is NOT a partition
// of unique customers and must not be labeled customer composition.
Online Customer Reach by Purchase Age =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Online Customers],
    CALCULATE(
        [Total Online Customers],
        REMOVEFILTERS(FactOnlineSales[AgeGroupAtPurchase])
    )
)

Online Sales Share by Purchase Age =
DIVIDE(
    [Online Sales],
    CALCULATE([Online Sales], REMOVEFILTERS(FactOnlineSales[AgeGroupAtPurchase]))
)
